    "chapter_name": "Current Electricity",
    "year": "2023",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical cells, when connected either in parallel or in series gives same current in an external resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The internal resistance of each cell will be ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;be the internal resistance of each cell.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0100_80eef768f85f.png\" style=\"width: 576px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p>In above shown figure, first represents the series connection of cells. Second and third figures represents the parallel connection&nbsp;of cells.</p><p>Now, in case of series connection, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></math>. So, current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#949;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;.....(1)</p><p>In case of parallel&nbsp;connection,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. So, current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#949;</mi><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;.....(2)</p><p>Equating (1) and (2), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#949;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#949;</mi><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
}